  "question": {
    "text": "The formation of molecular complex $\\mathrm{BF}_3-\\mathrm{NH}_3$ results in a change in hybridization of boron",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mjI21",
      "text": "\nfrom $s p^2$ to $d s p^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Bm7Al",
      "text": "\nfrom $s p^2$ to $s p^3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xJIKa",
      "text": "\nfrom $s p^3$ to $s p^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w2J2F",
      "text": "\nfrom $s p^3$ to $s p^3 d$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\operatorname{In~} \\mathrm{BF}_3, \\mathrm{~B}$ is $s p^2$ hybridized with one empty $p_{\\mathrm{z}}$ orbital. The empty $p_{\\mathrm{z}}$ orbital of $\\mathrm{BF}_3$ can be filled by lone pair of molecules such as $\\mathrm{NH}_3$. When this occurs a tetrahedral molecule or ion is formed which is $s p^3$ hybridized.",
    "image": null
  },
